From `tests/qa/testcase.py`, the 15 tests call `_drive_value(...)`, which always constructs a `Template`, creates `_ForEachValueRef(get_hash(ref_name), ref_name)`, and calls `.value(cfn, runtime_params)` once. In `_ForEachValueRef.value`, every call reaches the initial `params is None` handling, resolves `v`, checks `v in params`, skips `only_params`, computes `region/account_id/partition`, and then walks the AWS pseudo-parameter dispatch chain until a matching return, or falls through into parameter resolution. Taking the union of the branches exercised by the 15 test inputs in the QA file gives coverage of the initial setup lines, the gov and cn partition assignments, the heads and bodies for `AWS::Region`, `AWS::Partition`, `AWS::StackId`, `AWS::StackName`, `AWS::URLSuffix`, `AWS::NoValue`, the early runtime-params return, and the parameter-resolution paths for default string, default list, allowed-values string, allowed-values list, and list-without-default/allowed-values. The untested branches are the `AWS::AccountId` body, `AWS::NotificationARNs` body, the missing-parameter raise, the SSM raise, and the final non-list raise.

